      "analysis_source": "llm-per-reviewer",
      "patch_summary": "This patch reduces contention on the lru_lock by moving the calculation of scan-balance cost to the reclaim side, rather than having producers update the cost under lru_lock. It uses vmstat-derived counters (PGROTATE_ANON and PGROTATE_FILE) to calculate the cost, which are then folded into a per-lruvec accumulator under a dedicated lock. This approach eliminates the need for producers to re-acquire lru_lock and reduces contention on memory-pressured workloads."
